# Response headers for the portfolio.
#
# Read by hosts that support the `_headers` convention (Netlify, Cloudflare
# Pages) and ignored harmlessly by hosts that do not - so the directive set
# that a meta tag cannot express has to live here. The Content-Security-Policy
# below MUST stay in step with the <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy">
# in index.html: when either changes, change both, or the browser enforces the
# intersection of the two policies and the site breaks in confusing ways.
#
# index.html explains what each origin is for. All assets are self-hosted
# (including the icon-subset webfonts), and the two runtime reads that used to be
# third-party hosts — the Medium feed and the contributions calendar — now go to
# this site's own Functions (/api/medium, /api/contributions) instead, so they need
# no origin here. What is left in connect-src is what the browser itself must
# reach: the GitHub profile API and the Content Tracking Dashboard's own watchlist
# endpoint.
#
# contenttrackerdashboard.pages.dev is the dashboard section's one
# data source. It replaced docs.google.com and *.googleusercontent.com, which
# served the dashboard's Google Sheet: the dashboard moved to D1 and the Sheet
# stopped being its store, so a copy read from there was free to disagree with
# the dashboard it described - and did. The endpoint answers this origin and no
# other, so it is named one host at a time rather than with a wildcard; leave it
# out of connect-src and the section quietly falls back to its embedded
# snapshot instead of failing loudly.
#
# There is no medium.com origin in connect-src, and that is the point. The
# Writing-on-Medium cell reads /api/medium — this site's own Pages Function
# (functions/api/medium.js), which fetches Medium's feed server-side, where
# neither CORS nor the browser challenge applies, parses it and caches it for ten
# minutes. It used to read api.rss2json.com, a third-party JSON proxy: on 15 Oct
# 2026 that proxy answered HTTP 500 while Medium's own feed was returning 200
# with 10 items, so the cell was empty for every visitor and the page could do
# nothing about it. Same origin means no new origin here, and one fewer service
# that can take the section down.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://contenttrackerdashboard.pages.dev; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  # frame-ancestors is the one directive a <meta> tag cannot carry - it is what
  # actually stops the site being framed, so it is paired with the legacy
  # header below for engines that predate it.
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Nothing here uses a device API; denying them costs nothing and keeps a
  # future embedded widget from inheriting a permission the page never asked for.
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), bluetooth=(), serial=(), midi=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=(), accelerometer=()
  # Deliberately without includeSubDomains or preload: this pins HTTPS for this
  # host alone, which cannot strand a sibling host that is still HTTP-only.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Caching for the static assets. None of these filenames carry a content hash,
# so none of them can be `immutable` — a changed file has to be able to reach a
# returning visitor, and an immutable promise on a stable URL cannot be revoked.
# A week plus stale-while-revalidate gets the repeat visit off the network while
# leaving the next one free to pick up a new copy.
#
# Deliberately *not* applied to the HTML: index.html is the app, and a cached
# copy of it is how a deploy appears not to have happened.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400
